# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE?schema=SCHEMA
#
# Examples:
#   - Local dev:     postgresql://kwanza:kwanza@localhost:5432/kwanza_erp?schema=public
#   - Docker:        postgresql://kwanza:kwanza@postgres:5432/kwanza_erp?schema=public
#   - Supabase:      postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT.supabase.co:5432/postgres?schema=public
#   - Neon:          postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-NAME-REGION.aws.neon.tech/dbname?schema=public
#   - Railway:       postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@containers-us-west-1.railway.app:PORT/railway
#
# NOTE: The `?schema=public` suffix is recommended — it puts all tables in the
# `public` schema (the default). You can use a custom schema name if you want
# to isolate Kwanza from other apps in the same database.
#
# MIGRATION INSTRUCTIONS (SQLite → PostgreSQL):
#   1. Install PostgreSQL locally or provision a managed instance
#      (Supabase, Neon, Railway, Render all have free tiers).
#   2. Create a database named `kwanza_erp` (or whatever you prefer).
#   3. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your real connection string.
#   4. Run: npx prisma migrate dev --name init_from_sqlite
#      This creates all 36 tables + indexes in Postgres.
#   5. Run: npx tsx scripts/migrate-sqlite-to-postgres.ts
#      This reads your old SQLite DB (set OLD_SQLITE_URL below) and writes
#      all rows to Postgres, preserving IDs and createdAt timestamps.
#   6. Restart the dev server.
#
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://kwanza:kwanza@localhost:5432/kwanza_erp?schema=public"

# ── Legacy SQLite path (used ONLY by the one-time data migration script) ────
# Leave this pointing at your old SQLite file during the migration.
# After the migration succeeds, you can delete this variable and the .db file.
OLD_SQLITE_URL="file:/home/z/my-project/db/custom.db"
